# Trivy vulnerability scan suppressions.
#
# Suppressed entries are documented here with the reason and the
# condition for removing the suppression.
#
# Format: one CVE-ID per line. Optionally followed by an expiry comment.

# CVE-2026-23949 — jaraco.context path traversal via malicious tar archives.
#
# Status: FIXED upstream (patched in 6.1.0); our runtime image installs
# jaraco.context 6.1.2 and 1.2.0 trivy. However the base image
# (python:3.11-slim -> Debian 13 / trixie) also ships a *stale* copy at a
# path pip cannot reach: the dist-info directory remains after the
# passing packages and is reported by Trivy's crawler.
#
# Trivy still flags this via the UNC path when it walks the image
# filesystem. We suppress it here until Debian ships a package fix that
# properly purges the stale directory.
#
# Revisit: when a Debian 13 (trixie) update ships with updated
# dist-info cleanup, OR when Trivy fixes the UNC/UNC path misdetection.
CVE-2026-23949
